  "lineage": "Music of Balochistan across southwestern Pakistan, southeastern Iran and southern Afghanistan, transmitted by hereditary Luri and Domb musician castes and documented from the 1960s onward by Radio Pakistan Quetta and researchers such as Jean During, marked by the bowed spike-fiddle suroz shadowing the voice heterophonically, the plucked tanburag lute, double-flute nal and donali, dholak or dohol accompaniment, and repertoires spanning zahirig laments, epic sherwandi narrative and the trance-healing guati ceremony.",
